    {
      "id": "aggie_intro",
      "type": "custom",
      "position": { "x": 300, "y": -200 },
      "data": {
        "header": "Sector 3: The Mycelium Maze",
        "body": "<p>Aggie steps beneath the massive bioluminescent mushroom canopy of Sector 3. Towering damp Amanita caps filter the fading arena sunlight into a soft turquoise glow. Damp moss covers the soil, laced with thick white threads of mycelium.</p>",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "<p>An eerie wave of familiarity washes over you. It looks like home — the Petrified Forest where you and Britt grew up. But as you close your eyes and reach out to tune into the fungal network, a cold realization hits: <em>the vital life force of your home isn't here.</em> This is a manufactured arena simulation, and your <strong>Teleport Through Network</strong> skill fails to anchor.</p>"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "style": "quote",
            "content": "\"It looks like home... but it feels hollow. No matter. I can still speak to the roots.\""
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "<p>You crouch down, placing both palms against the damp soil to commune with the local plant life using your <strong>Speak with Plants</strong> affinity.</p>"
          }
        ],
        "ports": [
          {
            "id": "port_aggie_roll",
            "text": "COMMUNE WITH THE ROOT NETWORK",
            "subtext": "Roll 2d12 + Presence/Instinct (Speak with Plants)",
            "scores": {}
          }
        ]
      }
    },
